<id/09/0960/#concept> a <http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E55_Type>, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Tapioca"@en ;
    skos:broader <id/grp/grp_cereals_grains/#concept> ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300012960> ;
    skos:definition "a starch prepared from the cassava root (*Manihot*). The juice of the root deposits a white fecula, which, after being well washed and dried, constitutes what is called \"moussache.\" When the moussache is dried on hot plates, the grains partly burst, and the fecula agglomerates in irregular, semi-opaque, gum-like masses, and is then called tapioca. [P. L. Simmonds, The Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products (1892), scan p. 385]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q873761> ;
